Reconstruct the original contiguous WinMM parameter blocks before the MCI
backend writes status results or reads the resume end time. Ghidra split them
into unrelated C locals, so even successful commands consumed wrong stack bytes.
Original dd2h.exe, verified with objdump:
- CD_Check: 0x416677 passes ebp-0x14; 0x416691 writes item=3 at +8;
  0x4166a1 compares the returned track count at +4 with 19.
- Check_For_CD_Loop: 0x416250 passes ebp-0x1c; 0x41626a writes item=4
  at +8; 0x416272 compares the returned mode at +4 with MCI_MODE_PLAY.
- CD_Restart: 0x416329 writes dwTo at ebp-8, 0x41632c passes ebp-0x10
  (dwTo = +8), and MCI_PLAY carries only MCI_TO (flags=8). The callback
  and from fields are unused, as in the original.
Use real arrays with the original offsets; no fabricated track count, mode,
resume position, or new engine branch.

--- a/dd2.c
+++ b/dd2.c
